{
  "id": "insert-interval",
  "questionId": "insert-interval",
  "slug": "insert-interval",
  "title": "Insert Interval",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Merge intervals",
  "patterns": [
    "merge intervals",
    "sorting"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "blind-75",
    "grind-75",
    "interview-150"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "the existing list is already sorted with no overlaps - do you need to re-sort anything if you insert carefully?",
    "think of the result in three parts: intervals that end entirely before newInterval starts, intervals that overlap newInterval, and intervals that start entirely after newInterval ends",
    "copy the first part unchanged, then merge all overlapping intervals into newInterval by expanding its start to the min and its end to the max as you go, then copy the last part unchanged",
    "an interval overlaps newInterval when its start is <= newInterval's end AND its end is >= newInterval's start"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "re-sorting the whole list from scratch instead of exploiting that it's already sorted, which is unnecessary extra work but also easy to get wrong on the merge boundary",
    "using the wrong overlap condition and missing intervals that touch newInterval only at an endpoint",
    "forgetting to append the newly merged interval to the result before continuing with the remaining untouched intervals"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a list of intervals that is already sorted by start time and\ncontains no overlapping intervals, plus one new interval `newInterval`\nto insert, given as a length-2 array `[start, end]`.\n\n**Insert `newInterval` into the list, merging any overlaps as needed,\nand return the resulting list still sorted by start time with no\noverlaps.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "0 <= intervals.length <= 10^4",
      "intervals[i].length == 2 and newInterval.length == 2",
      "-10^4 <= starti <= endi <= 10^4 for every interval, including newInterval",
      "intervals is sorted by start and has no overlaps before inserting"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "intervals is empty",
      "newInterval doesn't overlap any existing interval and belongs at the very start or very end",
      "newInterval overlaps every existing interval, merging them all into one",
      "newInterval touches an existing interval exactly at an endpoint"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "intervals = [[1,3],[6,9]], newInterval = [2,5]",
        "output": "[[1,5],[6,9]]",
        "expectedOutput": "[[1,5],[6,9]]",
        "explanation": "[2,5] overlaps [1,3] and merges into [1,5]; [6,9] is untouched"
      },
      {
